op_reason":null,"evidence":["push.py:230 `except OSError as exc:` then `logger.warning(\"async tickets-branch push spawn failed: %r\", exc)`","enrich_drain.py:462 `except Exception:` then `logger.warning(\"enrich drain detach failed; continuing\", exc_info=True)`","compact_trigger.py:260 `except Exception:` then `logger.warning(\"compaction sweep detach failed; continuing\", exc_info=True)`","Plan Scope: helper 'would own … the never-raise posture; callers would supply the child entry point, their stderr sink, and their child ENV'"],"finding":"The plan folds three never-raise wrappers into one 'never-raise posture' owned by the helper, but the three sites do not catch identically: push.py catches only `except OSError` (logging `%r`), whereas enrich_drain and compact_trigger catch broad `except Exception` (logging with `exc_info=True`). A single helper-owned wrapper would silently change push.py's exposure (OSError-only → all exceptions), an unremarked behavior change.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc51b89e1889be5d4","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope bullet: 'The helper … would own … the never-raise posture'; AC 'none re-implements the bootstrap or the detach flags'","norm_id":"n88f64a69210481ec","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A non-OSError raised by Popen construction at the push site (previously propagating) is now swallowed by the shared wrapper","Reviewers checking behavior-preservation cannot tell whether push.py's narrower contract was intentionally widened"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Decide the boundary: let the helper build+spawn but RE-RAISE, with each caller keeping its existing catch (push.py `except OSError`, drain/sweep `except Exception`) and its own log line; or, if the helper is to own the catch, note explicitly in Scope that push.py's OSError-only posture is being intentionally broadened to Exception and confirm no caller relied on non-OSError propagation.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add an acceptance criterion for a behavioral test that `spawn_detached` preserves the caller-supplied env unchanged except for the PYTHONPATH layering — asserting push.py's secret-stripped projection (and `REBAR_SYNC_PUSH=always`) survive and no extra env leaks in.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.portability"],"criteria":["E5"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'the helper only layers the PYTHONPATH bootstrap onto whatever env the caller provides, so consolidation cannot drop push.py's secret-stripping'","AC #2 pins only that 'every detached spawn goes through it' (a structural anti-copy-paste test), not that the helper preserves the caller's env projection","The plan's central motivation is that a behavior (missing cwd) silently propagated across all three sites — the same silent-regression risk applies to the env-layering the helper now owns"],"finding":"The plan names push.py's secret-stripped env projection (`project_child_env(relationship=\"unrelated\")` + `REBAR_SYNC_PUSH=always`) versus the drain/sweep's plain `{**os.environ}` as a load-bearing invariant the consolidation 'cannot drop', but the Acceptance Criteria only pin a structural test that spawns route through the helper (AC #2). There is no acceptance criterion requiring a behavioral test that the helper preserves each caller's supplied env (and specifically that push.py's secret-stripped projection is not clobbered by the PYTHONPATH-bootstrap layering). Given the plan's own thesis — a defect silently replicated across all three sites — the env-preservation seam is exactly where a consolidation regression would hide.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fcc0fc280d6d8c470","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope first bullet ('env construction stays per-caller') + Acceptance Criteria #2","norm_id":"n0c890d66844479f6","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_dir